Tools of Trade Exemptions (§30.37(b)) 

Tools of trade are exempt from filing requirements if the item is: 

• Owned by the individual U.S. Principal Party in Interest (USPPI) or exporting company; 
• Accompanying the individual USPPI, employee, or representative of the exporting company; 
• Necessary, appropriate and intended for personal or business use; 
• Not for sale; 
• Returned to the U.S. within one year from the date of export; AND 
• Not shipped under a bill of lading or air waybill. 

